[1.509, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1.517, "o", "A simple package manager for pre-built binaries.\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mUsage:\u001b[0m \u001b[1m\u001b[32mocx\u001b[0m \u001b[36m[OPTIONS]\u001b[0m \u001b[36m[COMMAND]\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mCommands:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32menv\u001b[0m      Compose and print the toolchain environment\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32madd\u001b[0m      Add one or more package bindings to ocx.toml\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mclean\u001b[0m    Remove unreferenced objects from the local object store\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mconfig\u001b[0m   Manage the corporate managed-configuration tier\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mdirenv\u001b[0m   direnv integration (init writes .envrc; export emits the env block)\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mindex\u001b[0m    Inspect the package index and refresh the local copy\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mabout\u001b[0m    Print ocx version, registry, platform, shell, and home directory\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32minit\u001b[0m     Create a minimal ocx.toml in the current directory\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mlock\u001b[0m     Resolve package tags to digests and write ocx.lock\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mlogin\u001b[0m    Authenticate to a registry and persist credentials\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mlogout\u001b[0m   Remove credentials for a registry\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mupdate\u001b[0m   Re-resolve declared tags against the registry; the default group or a subset\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mupgrade\u001b[0m  Move declared tags in ocx.toml to the newest published release\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mpackage\u001b[0m  Operations related to packages (e.g. bundling or deploying)\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mpatch\u001b[0m    Manage patch overlays for a project\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mpull\u001b[0m     Pre-warm the object store, then render the project toolchain\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mremove\u001b[0m   Remove one or more package bindings from ocx.toml [alias: rm]\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mexec\u001b[0m     Run a command with the composed environment from the project toolchain [alias: x]\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mshell\u001b[0m    Open your shell inside the project environment\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mself\u001b[0m     Manage the OCX installation itself (PATH activation, completions, self-update)\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mstatus\u001b[0m   Show what ocx.toml and ocx.lock declare, without resolving anything\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32minspect\u001b[0m  Inspect what the project toolchain resolves to, without installing\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32mversion\u001b[0m  Print the version of ocx\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[33mOptions:\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m-c\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--config\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<FILE>\u001b[0m\r\n          Path to the ocx configuration file.\r\n          \r\n          Can also be set via the `OCX_CONFIG` environment variable. The file must exist, or the command exits 79. To disable config discovery entirely, set `OCX_NO_CONFIG=1`.\r\n          \r\n          The file layers on top of the discovered system, user and `$OCX_HOME` files and of the managed tier; it does not replace them.\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--project\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<PATH>\u001b[0m\r\n          Project directory, or the project file itself (project-tier toolchain config).\r\n          \r\n          A directory resolves to the `ocx.toml` inside it, so `--project .` and `--project /path/to/repo` both work; a file may have any name (like Cargo `--manifest-path`). Equivalent env var: `OCX_PROJECT`; `OCX_NO_PROJECT=1` disables project discovery.\r\n          \r\n          A path that does not exist exits 79, a directory with no `ocx.toml` exits 64, and an unreadable path exits 74.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m-g\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--global\u001b[0m\r\n          Select the global toolchain (`$OCX_HOME/ocx.toml`) as the project file in effect, instead of discovering a project by CWD walk.\r\n          \r\n          Mutually exclusive with `--project`. Applies to this invocation only: a child ocx process selects its own tier.\r\n          \r\n          The global toolchain never composes into project resolution; `ocx exec` and `ocx package exec` stay hermetic and never read it.\r\n          \r\n          Before the subcommand `-g` means `--global`; after it, `-g` means `--group`. Nothing selects the global toolchain implicitly.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m-r\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--remote\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.517, "o", "          Route mutable lookups (tag list, catalog, tag->manifest) to the remote registry instead of the local index.\r\n          \r\n          Pure queries (`index list`, `index catalog`, `package description pull`) do **not** persist the result to the local index - use `ocx index update` to refresh the local index explicitly. Implies network access.\r\n          \r\n          Combined with `--offline` the result is \"pinned-only mode\": no source contact. Any tag-addressed resolution that cannot be satisfied locally errors instead of silently falling back. Equivalent env var: `OCX_REMOTE`.\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--offline\u001b[0m\r\n          Disable all network access.\r\n          \r\n          Tag->digest resolution must be satisfied by the local index or a digest-pinned identifier; unpinned tags missing from the local index exit 81. Run `ocx index update` online first, or switch to a digest-pinned identifier. Useful for hermetic CI runs and air-gapped environments.\r\n          \r\n          Equivalent env var: `OCX_OFFLINE`.\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--frozen\u001b[0m\r\n          Freeze tag resolution to the local index; never fetch an unknown tag.\r\n          \r\n          A tag in the local index resolves from cache. A digest-pinned reference (or a tag `ocx.lock` pins) still fetches its content. An unpinned tag missing from the index errors. Populate the index first with `ocx index update` (refused under this flag, exit 81).\r\n          \r\n          Scoped to packages: patch companions and managed configuration still resolve live. Unlike `--offline` and Cargo's `--frozen`, the network stays reachable for known content.\r\n          \r\n          Conflicts with `--remote`. Env var: `OCX_FROZEN`.\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--format\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<FORMAT>\u001b[0m\r\n          Output format for stdout reports: `plain` (default) or `json`.\r\n          \r\n          Applies to every command; there is no per-command `--format`. The `--shell[=NAME]` output of `env` / `package env` is unaffected. Each report's fields are in the reports schema, <https://ocx.sh/schemas/reports/v1.json>.\r\n          \r\n          [possible values: json, plain]\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--json\u001b[0m\r\n          Shorthand for `--format json`.\r\n          \r\n          Last one wins if combined with `--format`.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m-q\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--quiet\u001b[0m\r\n          Suppress the stdout report and progress bars (errors and warnings remain).\r\n          \r\n          When set, the CLI's structured report (table or JSON) is not printed and no transfer progress is rendered on stderr. Equiv"]
[1.517, "o", "alent env var: `OCX_QUIET`.\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--jobs\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<N>\u001b[0m\r\n          Maximum number of root packages to pull concurrently.\r\n          \r\n          `0` means \"use all logical cores\" (GNU Parallel convention). Omitting the flag falls back to the `OCX_JOBS` environment variable; when neither is set, pulls run unbounded.\r\n          \r\n          Negative values are rejected at parse time.\r\n          \r\n          Caps only the outer dispatch - transitive dependency and layer extraction stay unbounded.\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--index\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<PATH>\u001b[0m\r\n          Overrides the local index home directory.\r\n          "]
[1.517, "o", "\r\n          The local index is a collection of per-source subtrees, one per configured registry or index, each holding tag roots plus their manifest data. Resolution can work fully offline once it is populated. This flag redirects the whole collection, replacing the default at `$OCX_HOME/index`.\r\n          \r\n          Digest-addressed lookups still consult the local index even under `--remote`; only tag listings and tag->manifest lookups route to the remote registry there. Can also be set via the `OCX_INDEX` environment variable.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m-l\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--log-level\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<LOG_LEVEL>\u001b[0m\r\n          The log level to use.\r\n          \r\n          Default `info`. Logs go to stderr, never stdout. At `info` and below a line reads `error: message` or `warning: message`; `debug` and `trace` add a timestamp and level. Can also be set via the `OCX_LOG_LEVEL` environment variable.\r\n          \r\n          [possible values: trace, debug, info, warn, error, off]\r\n\r\n      \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--color\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m<WHEN>\u001b[0m\r\n          When to use ANSI colors in output.\r\n          \r\n          Default `auto`: color only on a terminal. An explicit `--color` outranks `NO_COLOR`, `CLICOLOR` and `CLICOLOR_FORCE`.\r\n          \r\n"]
[1.517, "o", "          [default: auto]\r\n          [possible values: auto, always, never]\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1m\u001b[32m-h\u001b[0m, \u001b[1m\u001b[32m--help\u001b[0m\r\n          Print help (see a summary with '-h')\r\n"]
[1.519, "o", "\u001b[?2004h$ "]
[3.021, "o", "exit\r\n"]
[3.021, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[3.021, "o", "exit\r\n"]
